The best response came from Whitney Latta as follows:-

As of V5.1B-3, new_wire_method is no longer configurable, and is
hardcoded enabled (1). You cannot check it with sysconfig (it will
return "unknown attribute"), but you can check it by using dbx:

As root, type "dbx -k /vmunix"
At the dbx> prompt, type "p new_wire_method"

root > dbx -k /vmunix
dbx version 5.1
Type 'help' for help.

stopped at  [thread_block:3317 ,0xffffffff000bb7c0]      Source not
available

warning: Files compiled -g3: parameter values probably wrong
(dbx) p new_wire_method
1
(dbx) quit
root >=20



The ability to configure new_wire_method has een removed to eliminate
any lingering confusion regarding its use... Oracle and HP Tru64 unix
engineering has fully tested this and verifies it works as intended;
hence it is always enabled.

I hope this is helpful.

Regards,

